# sbt 2 runs every command through the thin client (sbtn). For such a command, sbt 2's `runMain`,
# which mdoc runs on, by default only hands the run over to the client and returns at once, so
# a task that ran `compileDocs` and then read website/docs found nothing there yet. Each command
# below runs one task the way a thin-client command would, starting from an empty website/docs.

$ absent website/docs/index.md
> compileDocsFromThinClient
$ exists website/docs/index.md
$ exec grep -q 'answer: Int = 42' website/docs/index.md

$ delete website/docs
> generateReadmeFromThinClient
$ exists README.md
$ exec grep -q 'answer: Int = 42' README.md
